  "notes": [
    "fill_id = '<time>:<coin>:<tid>' (SPEC dedupe key (time, coin, tid); docs: 'For a globally unique trade id, use (block_time, coin, tid)'). Spot coins look like '@107', HIP-3 coins like 'xyz:XYZ100' (contains ':'), so parse fill_id right-to-left if ever needed.",
    "Fee sign: 'negative means rebate' -> kept as-is. fee includes builderFee (doc comment).",
    "crossed=true -> taker, false -> maker. side 'B' -> buy, 'A' -> sell.",
    "The reconnect snapshot (isSnapshot true) repeats fill tid 228000000000001 -> dedupe_dropped 1.",
    "WsBasicOrder has no tif/orderType: tif is 'other' unless the status implies it (badAloPxRejected -> post_only; iocCancelRejected -> ioc). historicalOrders carries orderType/tif if a richer import is needed.",
    "WsBasicOrder.sz is the REMAINING size; origSz is the order size -> orig_qty/qty_str from origSz.",
    "modify is cancel + new order with a new oid (exchange-endpoint text: always_place / cancel semantics). C1 and C2 are separate order_keys sharing cloid; the canonical schema has no field linking them, so the price change cannot become a 5.7.2 'new leg' of one order (SPEC gap).",
    "Snapshot fills for orders never seen in orderUpdates (Z, spot 90999999998) -> fills-only orders (unmatched_fills 2).",
    "statusTimestamp -> record_time; fill time -> match_time."
  ],
